<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<pretext xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <docinfo>
    <numbering>
      <equations level="1"/>
    </numbering>
  </docinfo>

  <article xml:id="test-subequations">
    <title>Test: Subequations (mds)</title>

    <section xml:id="sec-basic">
      <title>Basic Subequations</title>

      <p>A regular numbered equation before the subequation block:</p>
      <men xml:id="eq-before">
        E = mc^2
      </men>

      <p>Now a block of subequations (Maxwell's equations):</p>
      <mds xml:id="eq-maxwell">
        <mrow xml:id="eq-gauss-e">\nabla \cdot \mathbf{E} \amp= \frac{\rho}{\epsilon_0}</mrow>
        <mrow xml:id="eq-gauss-m">\nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} \amp= 0</mrow>
        <mrow xml:id="eq-faraday">\nabla \times \mathbf{E} \amp= -\frac{\partial \mathbf{B}}{\partial t}</mrow>
        <mrow xml:id="eq-ampere">\nabla \times \mathbf{B} \amp= \mu_0 \mathbf{J} + \mu_0 \epsilon_0 \frac{\partial \mathbf{E}}{\partial t}</mrow>
      </mds>

      <p>And a regular equation after:</p>
      <men xml:id="eq-after">
        F = ma
      </men>

      <p>Cross-reference tests:
        The full group is <xref ref="eq-maxwell"/>.
        Gauss's law for electricity is <xref ref="eq-gauss-e"/>.
        Faraday's law is <xref ref="eq-faraday"/>.
        The equation before is <xref ref="eq-before"/>
        and the one after is <xref ref="eq-after"/>.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section xml:id="sec-second-block">
      <title>Multiple Blocks and Gather</title>

      <p>A second subequation block using gather alignment (no ampersands):</p>
      <mds xml:id="eq-kinematics" alignment="gather">
        <mrow xml:id="eq-vel">v = v_0 + at</mrow>
        <mrow xml:id="eq-pos">x = x_0 + v_0 t + \tfrac{1}{2}at^2</mrow>
        <mrow xml:id="eq-vsq">v^2 = v_0^2 + 2a(x - x_0)</mrow>
      </mds>

      <p>Reference to position equation: <xref ref="eq-pos"/>.</p>

    </section>

  </article>
</pretext>
